{
  // SARBAN plan 1 of 2 — engine correctness, Telegram, versioning + update.
  // The annotated master brief is docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md (plan set strips these comments).
  "name": "Sarban core - the engine says what it knows",
  "repo": "C:/code/conductor",
  "tracker": "SARBAN-CORE-TRACKER.md",
  "planDoc": "docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md",
  "branchPattern": "^feat/sarban$",
  "pauseOnBlocked": true,
  "batteryCollapse": false,

  "agent": {
    "command": "claude",
    "model": "claude-opus-5",
    "args": [
      "-p", "{prompt}",
      "--output-format", "stream-json",
      "--verbose",
      "--dangerously-skip-permissions",
      "--model", "{model}",
      "--session-id", "{sessionId}"
    ],
    "resumeArgs": [
      "-p", "{prompt}",
      "--output-format", "stream-json",
      "--verbose",
      "--dangerously-skip-permissions",
      "--model", "{model}",
      "--resume", "{claudeSessionId}"
    ],
    "output": "stream-json"
  },

  "advisor": {
    "enabled": true,
    "command": "claude",
    "args": ["-p", "{prompt}", "--output-format", "json", "--model", "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"],
    "output": "json",
    "timeoutMinutes": 6
  },

  "defaultWorkflow": "deliver",
  "workflows": {
    "deliver": {
      "name": "deliver",
      "description": "Deliver until the stage's checkpoints are confirmed; fix only when gates are red.",
      "repeat": true,
      "steps": [
        { "id": "deliver", "kind": "Deliver", "deliver": true },
        { "id": "fix-if-red", "kind": "Fix", "deliver": true, "runIf": "!gatesGreen" }
      ]
    }
  },

  "templatesDir": "sarban-templates",

  "setup": {
    "command": "dotnet build-server shutdown; exit 0",
    "timeoutMinutes": 2
  },
  "teardown": {
    "command": "dotnet build-server shutdown; exit 0",
    "timeoutMinutes": 2
  },

  "stages": [
    {
      "id": "SC1",
      "title": "Telegram actually delivers",
      "sessions": 2,
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md section SC1. Root cause is cited there: nothing ever starts the hosted service - RunCommand resolves the Orchestrator straight from the container, so _started stays false and every push is silently dropped while the test button works. Follow the ControlPlaneServer precedent of an explicit start. Acceptance: a real run path delivers a real push, two-way answers, and a regression test drives the actual run-start path. The live proof is a nested run of YOUR build against a scratch repo (promptExtra trap 2) - CONDUCTOR_TELEGRAM_TOKEN must be present in your environment; the owner sets it before launch. If the token is genuinely absent, record a HUMAN: line and park - never mock the push to claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "SC2",
      "title": "Truthful surfaces",
      "sessions": 3,
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md section SC2. Status never calls a healthy run interrupted; sticky failure fields age or clear; one canonical gates GREEN or RED vocabulary on phase-gate lines plus an honest no-gates-configured confirmation state and consistent attempt numbering; /state carries in-flight and window-vs-lifetime spend; RUN-SUMMARY.md on completion, offline report and status, shared-read log, incremental SSE tails."
    },
    {
      "id": "SC3",
      "title": "Config traps die at authoring time",
      "sessions": 3,
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md section SC3. Doctor FAILS on a dropped model token; unknown RunIf and SkipIf tokens fail at plan load; plan set refuses absent leaf keys, suggests the dotted path, and reaches the live engine or says how; a literal brace in plan prose is caught by doctor and parks at runtime instead of a silent stderr-only exit, with a double-brace escape; advisor defaults work headless or refuse loudly, and plan-config.md stops documenting a default that does not exist."
    },
    {
      "id": "SC4",
      "title": "Verdicts judge the work, not the environment",
      "sessions": 3,
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md section SC4. Settle before the battery and retry a red required gate once before GatesRed; NoProgress requires no commits AND no newly-DONE checkpoints, with conductor's own chore commits excluded from the count; satelliteRepos for multi-repo diffs and gate-cache keys that cover the gate's own working directory and command text; injections render at the top of the prompt and supersede a stale gate-failures block."
    },
    {
      "id": "SC5",
      "title": "The engine can wait, detach, and correct the board",
      "sessions": 3,
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md section SC5. Blocked-until as a first-class session outcome the run loop honours by sleeping and respawning once, surfaced everywhere; run --detach prints pid and control-plane url and survives its launching shell; task --todo --blocked --skipped --amend land through the shared writes path and --in-progress reports the post-fold truth; bg rows map to their session stream and runtimes use one timezone. Prove detach and blocked-until with YOUR build against a scratch repo (promptExtra trap 2) - never by aiming run verbs at this repo."
    },
    {
      "id": "SC6",
      "title": "Clean history without lying about it",
      "sessions": 2,
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md section SC6. Pure status-transition commits stop landing; any squash runs AFTER the final state write, works on a dirty tree, reports real counts, logs git stderr and exit code on failure, un-marks the stage on failure instead of permanently marking it squashed, aborts a half-started rebase, and degrades gracefully off Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "SC7",
      "title": "The transcript captures structure",
      "sessions": 3,
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md section SC7. Store tool events structured - name plus extracted fields, values truncated, JSON never cut - with back-compat reading of the old lines; note writes outside the repo in the verdict; emit readable one-liner wire lines from the provider and compute, store and serve a per-session digest. The worked example in the spec is the acceptance shape. This stage enables the whole face round."
    },
    {
      "id": "SC8",
      "title": "The program knows what it is and can update itself",
      "sessions": 3,
      "notes": "SPEC: docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md section SC8. A version verb and /version endpoint stamped at build with semver, git sha and date; automatic tag-height versioning reconciled with the release workflow so a downloaded binary answers with its tag; install.ps1 prints before and after versions; CHANGELOG per release; conductor update checks the latest release and swaps binaries safely, refusing while a run is live; doctor reports update-available. Prove the swap against a scratch copy of an installed engine - never the live published one driving you (promptExtra traps 1 and 2)."
    }
  ],

  "gatePolicy": "perPhase",
  "gates": [
    { "name": "engine-fast", "command": "dotnet build Conductor.slnx -clp:ErrorsOnly", "tier": "fast", "timeoutMinutes": 15 },
    { "name": "face-fast", "command": "cmd /c \"cd /d C:\\code\\conductor\\face-go && go build ./... && go vet ./...\"", "tier": "fast", "timeoutMinutes": 10 },
    { "name": "engine-full", "command": "dotnet test Conductor.slnx", "tier": "full", "timeoutMinutes": 40 },
    { "name": "face-full", "command": "cmd /c \"cd /d C:\\code\\conductor\\face-go && go test ./...\"", "tier": "full", "timeoutMinutes": 15 }
  ],

  "limits": {
    "stallMinutes": 15,
    "sessionTimeoutMinutes": 120,
    "maxResumesPerSession": 2,
    "stageSlackFactor": 2,
    "backoffMinutes": 30,
    "maxBackoffs": 10,
    "maxRunCostUsd": 260
  },

  "report": { "commit": false, "push": false },

  // Push-only until SC1 lands (the CURRENT engine never starts the service - that is the point
  // of SC1). Token lives in env CONDUCTOR_TELEGRAM_TOKEN or .conductor/secrets.local.json.
  "telegram": { "allowedChatIds": ["99205495"], "pollIntervalSeconds": 4, "enableTwoWay": true },

  "readOrder": [
    "docs/history/CONDUCTOR-SARBAN.md"
  ],

  "promptExtra": "TRAPS THIS REPO HAS ALREADY PAID FOR, in order of cost:\n1. NEVER run tools/install.ps1 or overwrite the published engine - the conductor driving you runs from that published copy. The owner reinstalls between plans.\n2. This repo's .conductor/ is the LIVE state of the run driving you. The claim and note verbs (conductor task, note, bug, bg) and read-only verbs (status, task --list) are yours; NEVER aim run-control verbs (run, pause, resume, abort, approve, plan set, plan reload, goto, skip, retry-stage, rollback, kill) at this repo. Any live-run proof spawns YOUR build against a scratch repo with its own tiny plan and its own .conductor - for example under %TEMP%\\sarban-proofs - never against C:/code/conductor.\n3. The conductor on PATH is the OLD published engine - the one driving you. Exercise YOUR changes through the fresh build: dotnet run --project src/Conductor -- VERB, or the exe it builds. Testing a new verb through the PATH shim only proves the old engine lacks it. Exception by design: task claims go through the PATH copy, because they target the driving run.\n4. The ratchet gate is tools/gates/ratchet.ps1 - the wrong path prints an error but exits 0, a silent false green. Never raise the pragma ceiling; fix the cause instead, as DoctorCommand's AsyncCommand conversion did.\n5. face-go: pad plain text then style, never width-format an ANSI string; clamp with MaxWidth and MaxHeight; goldens pin UTC and live in face-go/internal/tui/testdata/golden - regenerate them in a separate rebaseline commit, and read face-go/STYLE.md before any face change.\n6. Orphaned dotnet test hosts flake the full suite; stopping stray dotnet processes between full runs is sanctioned, but never kill the conductor process itself.\n7. PowerShell tooling targets Windows PowerShell 5.1 and must stay ASCII-only - em-dashes have torn string literals here before.\n8. Keep tracker handoffs, checkpoint titles and all plan prose free of curly braces - a literal brace token reaches the composed prompt and kills the CURRENT engine at the stage boundary. SC3.3 fixes this; until the owner reinstalls the fixed engine, the discipline stands.\n9. The conductor MCP task tools may arrive deferred in your harness - ToolSearch for task_update first, or use the CLI: conductor task --done ID --evidence PATH. That command is the only claim; prose moves nothing.\n10. Commit per checkpoint with the repo's trailer convention and push feat/sarban. Go sources are checked out LF; keep them that way."
}
